 "gauge": "Waddy Point (K'gari)",
 "note": "Waddy Point (24 58 S 153 21 E) is on the open-ocean coast of K'gari, 114 km south-south-east. MSQ lists Lady Elliot Island as a secondary place of Bundaberg (Burnett Heads, 80 km south-south-west, at the mouth of the Burnett River) with high water 24 and low water 33 minutes earlier and 0.74 of its range. Waddy Point's tide runs about 25 minutes ahead of Burnett Heads' (M2 phase 12 degrees earlier in the 2026 fit), the same as Lady Elliot's, and its spring range about mean sea level (MHWS +0.63, MLWS -0.62 m) is closer to Lady Elliot's (+0.87, -0.86 m) than Burnett Heads' (+1.16, -1.17 m), so the open-coast gauge is the closer match. Heights at the island are still about a third larger than Waddy Point's.",
